# MANU-AI Execution Governance

Before implementation, read:

- `AGENTS.md`
- `docs/execution-governance/EXECUTION_ASSURANCE_PROTOCOL.md`
- `docs/execution-governance/MANU_AI_PLAN_IMPLEMENTATION_ASSURANCE_INTEGRATION_PLAN.md`

Rules:

- Work only inside the active plan scope.
- Do not reinterpret, narrow, or broaden plan requirements.
- If no active locked plan exists, product writes are blocked. Read-only exploration and governance-file work are allowed.
- Do not change product code, migrations, package manifests, lockfiles, verifier scripts, fixtures, baselines, CI, hooks, or production gates unless the active plan explicitly allows it.
- Do not push, merge, PR, deploy, enable provider/channel egress, enable live billing, roll out production schema, or process real health data.
- Run the exact executor checks required by the plan. Skipped, stale, blocked, or unrun checks are not PASS.
- Independent review is user-triggered only. Do not ask whether to review; record `NOT_REQUESTED` when the user has not requested it.
- You may report `IMPLEMENTED_UNVERIFIED` or executor check results. You may not claim independent review PASS for your own implementation.
- If you need scope expansion, stop before editing and create a scope-change request.
- If you need verifier or acceptance changes, stop before editing and create a verifier-change request.
- Do not create a review record when independent review was not requested by the user.
